</p/><p><strong>Summary: </strong>
Part of game culture is re-mixing and accumulating a toolbox of cool tech.
</p>
        <p><time datetime="2026-07-21" title="2026-07-21">Yesterday</time> I stumbled upon Mick’s <a href="https://advancedmysteryandmanners.blogspot.com/2026/06/together-through-ages-of-world.html">Advanced Mystery &amp; Manners: Together Through
Ages of the World…</a>.  In which the author shared <a href="https://wiseblood-games.itch.io/the-long-defeat">The Long Defeat</a>, a hack of
<cite><a href="https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/484480/mothership-deluxe-set-bundle?affiliate_id=318171">Mothership</a></cite> <small><a class="ref" rel="tag opener" aria-label="Other site-wide references of “Mothership”" title="Other site-wide references of “Mothership”" href="https://takeonrules.com/site-map/glossary/#abbr-dfn-GLOSSARY-MOTHERSHIP">&#128214;</a></small>
, that can swap out the rules engine of <cite><a href="https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/370267/The-One-RingTM-Core-Rules?affiliate_id=318171">The One Ring</a></cite> <small><a class="ref" rel="tag opener" aria-label="Other site-wide references of “The One Ring”" title="Other site-wide references of “The One Ring”" href="https://takeonrules.com/site-map/glossary/#abbr-dfn-GLOSSARY-TOR">&#128214;</a></small>
, while preserving
much of the source material of that system.</p>
<p>Having recently picked up <cite>Mothership</cite>
 and having played solo sessions—The Travels
of Duinhir Tailwind— of <cite>The One Ring</cite>
, I was curious.  I downloaded the 10 or so
page manual and gave it a read.  And it does seem to do a good job at rules
distillation.</p>
<p>From there, I pulled out the <cite>Warden’s Manual</cite>of <cite>Mothership</cite>
 and
started reading.  I’m not one for horror in movies, but invariably, I find
myself drawn to how I might invoke dread and fear in role-playing games.  And
the <cite>Warden’s Manual</cite>provides that guidance and more.</p>
<p>I found myself nodding along with Mick’s analysis; namely that the narrative
procedures and game pillars of <cite>Mothership</cite>
 align well with Tolkien’s narrative
arc of Middle Earth.</p>
<p>I think of the era of d20, in which we saw a rush towards universal systems.
And contrast to this era, where we have a plethora of available systems, and can
connect “tech” from different systems to different “genres” to try to tease out
something that works for our individual play cultures.</p>
<p>Yet it goes beyond that.  <a href="https://wiseblood-games.itch.io/the-long-defeat">The Long Defeat</a> is what happens when designers don’t
simply put forward mechanics, but also bring forward agendas and principles—to
invoke <span><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Powered_by_the_Apocalypse">Powered by the Apocalypse</a></span> (<abbr title="Powered by the Apocalypse">PbtA</abbr> <small><a class="ref" rel="tag opener" aria-label="Other site-wide references of “Powered by the Apocalypse”" title="Other site-wide references of “Powered by the Apocalypse”" href="https://takeonrules.com/site-map/glossary/#abbr-dfn-GLOSSARY-PBTA">&#128214;</a></small>)
-from which they then build approaches and considerations for running
the game.</p>
<p>We have, for awhile now, been in an era of visibility regarding <span><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Role-playing_game">Role Playing Games</a></span> (<abbr title="Role Playing Games">RPGs</abbr> <small><a class="ref" rel="tag opener" aria-label="Other site-wide references of “Role Playing Games”" title="Other site-wide references of “Role Playing Games”" href="https://takeonrules.com/site-map/glossary/#abbr-dfn-GLOSSARY-RPG">&#128214;</a></small>)
.  We have
open source systems, session reports, actual play recordings, discourse about
game-play, and academic studies of these games of ours.  I think to my personal
style of facilitating games, something that I developed by way playing in games
run by other people; and often those others were ones that were players in my
games.</p>
<p>Meaning we created a localized play culture.  From which I developed the
foundations of how I facilitate games.  And overtime, as I’ve studied other
folks approaches, I’ve metabolized some of those approaches.  Assembling a
person toolkit of approaches.  And <a href="https://wiseblood-games.itch.io/the-long-defeat">The Long Defeat</a> is that mindset, now codified
into a playtest document.</p>

